WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.220
Kristofer Hivju plays Tormund Giantsbane in
Game of Thrones, the big-bearded Wildling

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.260
leader with a soft spot for Brienne of Tarth.

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:11.620
Hivju's character has quickly become a fan
favorite, but what else has the Norwegian

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.460
actor appeared in?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.280
Why does he look so familiar?

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:15.760
The Thing

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.980
Although he had appeared on a few Norwegian
TV shows and one feature film, Hivju's break

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:26.230
into international cinema came when he was
cast as one of the Arctic researchers in 2011's

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.800
The Thing, a prequel to the 1982 John Carpenter
classic.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.660
Hivju's turn in the widely panned horror flick
didn't win him any awards, but it put him

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.969
on American casting directors' radar, setting
the wheels in motion for his eventual role

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:40.740
on Game of Thrones in 2013.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.320
After Earth

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:48.030
The Thing may not have lived up to expectations,
but Hivju's next movie, 2013's After Earth,

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:52.800
gave him a real crash course in how badly
things can go wrong for a major motion picture.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.900
Problems started for the actor when he showed
up on set and the makeup artists decided to

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.440
cut off his long hair and bushy beard — a
decision he fought, even getting star Jaden

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.420
Smith to back him up, but the makeup crew
won in the end.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.620
After Earth was mauled critically, so maybe
losing the beard was worth it — it makes

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.080
him harder to recognize in a movie he'd probably
rather forget.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.440
Force Majeure

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:19.500
Hivju returned to his Scandinavian roots with
2014's Force Majeure, a dark comedy that follows

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.020
a downtrodden husband in an unhappy marriage.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.540
Hivju, who plays the best friend character,
told Scan magazine it was a refreshing change

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:27.060
of pace:

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.500
"I didn't have a sword in my hand, I wasn't
climbing an ice wall, but playing a normal

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.040
man.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.700
As an actor you always want to be extraordinary,
but to play an ordinary man is a really big

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.260
challenge."

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:40.380
That challenge had a huge payoff: Hivju took
the award for Best Supporting Actor at the

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.780
Scandinavian equivalent to the Oscars in 2015.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.720
In Order Of Disappearance

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:51.180
That same year, Hivju played a gangster who
gets beaten up by Swedish acting legend Stellan

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.280
Skarsgard in the darkly funny revenge drama
In Order of Disappearance.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.200
The movie follows a father who goes after
a local drug gang in revenge for killing his

00:01:59.200 --> 00:01:59.720
son.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.980
The film, acclaimed for its artful blend of
black comedy and bloody violence, has been

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.740
described as a Scandinavian version of Fargo.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:07.980
Lilyhammer

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:13.940
Hivju rounded out a busy 2014 with a part
in Netflix's Norwegian-American crime-drama

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:18.070
Lilyhammer, which follows a former American
mafia boss hiding out in Norway.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:22.710
Hivju appeared in the episode "Foreign Affairs,"
in a small role as a Greenpeace worker.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:27.290
Sharp-eyed viewers may have noticed an allusion
to Hivju's Game of Thrones gig: during one

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.080
scene, a television clearly shows Hivju as
Tormund in a scene from the HBO hit.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.460
The Last King

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.080
In 2016, Hivju got to act out one of the most
important events in Norwegian history: the

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.590
protection of a future king during the Norwegian
Civil Wars by a group of patriotic warriors.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:49.440
Hivju grew up learning the 11th century story
that inspired The Last King in school, and

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.680
he was excited about the role.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.440
The characters in the movie spend a lot of
time on skis, believe it or not, since that

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.400
was the fastest way for medieval Norwegians
to get around — which led to some risky

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.480
stunts for Hivju.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.120
Beck

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.520
The Scandinavian police procedural Beck has
gone through many changes during its 20-year

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.200
run, including casting Hivju as the new partner
of the show's namesake police detective Martin

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:12.720
Beck.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:23.150
As a longtime fan of the show, Hivju eagerly
accepted the chance to join the cast, telling

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.090
Scan magazine before he got the gig,

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:29.260
"I have played many bad guys and villainous
roles, so to play a cop will be great fun

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:30.100
and very cool!"

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.000
The Fate of the Furious

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.860
Hivju's most high-profile movie role came
courtesy of 2017's The Fate of the Furious,

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.150
in which he played Connor Rhodes, right-hand
man and muscle for main villain Cipher, played

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.220
by Charlize Theron.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.790
Hivju was a huge fan of the Fast and Furious
franchise before he got his chance to join

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.520
it — and he also wasn't the only Game of
Thrones star in the movie.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.900
Nathalie Emmanuel, who plays Missandei, returned
as Ramsey, the Crew's hacker.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.680
Wyndham Rewards Commercials

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.780
Now, while Hivju usually plays dark, violent
roles, he can also be silly when necessary

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:07.100
— like when he started playing the eccentric,
wild-eyed Wyndham Rewards Wizard in the hotel

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.640
chain's string of commercials — clearly
the greatest part of his career.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:11.780
Not convinced?

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:12.880
Observe:

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.380
"Are we in the future?"

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:20.200
"Actually, we're in Branson, Missouri, and
now you've got all the breakfast you can eat!"

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.500
"Yeah!

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:22.700
Waffles!"

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:24.760
Thanks for watching!

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.810
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

